>>> E15  BREAK-EVEN - administration versus concrete
  No capital-cost figure is invented here. Instead each physical
  intervention is expressed as the administrative reform it would
  have to beat. Raballand et al. (2012) make the same argument for
  ports: speeding up clearance raises capacity far more cheaply
  than building more of it.

  intervention             | kind           | detention saved | vs best admin
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  digitalise all admin     | procedure      |         +8.98 h |         170%
  digitalise M5+M6         | procedure      |         +7.65 h |         145%
  terminal works 24/7      | procedure      |         +5.28 h |         100%
  all calendars 24/7       | procedure      |         +5.28 h |         100%
  +50% loading rate        | CAPITAL        |         +2.08 h |          39%
  no rework anywhere       | procedure      |         +1.40 h |          27%
  2nd line + 2nd crew      | CAPITAL        |         +0.58 h |          11%
  2nd shunting loco        | CAPITAL        |         -0.00 h |          -0%
  2nd loading line         | CAPITAL        |         -0.28 h |          -5%

